[32m+[m[32mChanges from 3.6.0 to 3.6.1[m
[32m+[m[32m===========================[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis is a bugfix and performance release that optimizes read-ahead prefetching[m
[32m+[m[32mfor memory-mapped frames on GPFS (IBM Storage Scale), avoiding page faults by[m
[32m+[m[32mpopulating mappings with `madvise(MADV_POPULATE_READ)` on Linux.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m* **Prefetching on GPFS via memory mapping population**: For frames read through[m
[32m+[m[32m  the mmap I/O backend (`BLOSC2_IO_FILESYSTEM_MMAP`) on GPFS, read-ahead threads now[m
[32m+[m[32m  populate the mapping directly using `madvise(MADV_POPULATE_READ)` (Linux >= 5.14)[m
[32m+[m[32m  instead of `read()`. Because GPFS caches read data in its internal pagepool rather[m
[32m+[m[32m  than the kernel page cache, populating the mapping avoids costly page faults and[m
[32m+[m[32m  speeds up multi-dimensional slice reads by 1.10x–1.34x (#880).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m* **Cached filesystem type checks**: Filesystem type queries via `statx()` are now[m
[32m+[m[32m  cached per thread across the last 4 accessed devices. This avoids redundant[m
[32m+[m[32m  `fstatfs()` RPC roundtrips to servers on remote filesystems such as NFS, preventing[m
[32m+[m[32m  I/O latency regressions on cached patch reads (#880).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m* **Kernel `MADV_POPULATE_READ` runtime detection**: Added a one-time per-process probe[m
[32m+[m[32m  to verify kernel support for `MADV_POPULATE_READ`. When unsupported (Linux < 5.14),[m
[32m+[m[32m  read-ahead threads safely fall back to reading chunks without issuing superfluous[m
[32m+[m[32m  page-cache queries via `cachestat()` (#880).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m* **New `BLOSC_PREFETCH_POPULATE` environment variable**: Setting[m
[32m+[m[32m  `BLOSC_PREFETCH_POPULATE=1` forces memory-mapped frame prefetching to populate[m
[32m+[m[32m  mappings via `madvise(MADV_POPULATE_READ)` across all filesystems, while `0`[m
[32m+[m[32m  disables it completely (#880).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m* **Fixed test build under Clang on Linux**: Defined `_GNU_SOURCE` in[m
[32m+[m[32m  `tests/b2nd/test_b2nd_prefetch.c` so `madvise()` is exposed when building with Clang[m
[32m+[m[32m  under `-D_XOPEN_SOURCE=600` (#880).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mChanges from 3.5.0 to 3.6.0[m
[32m+[m[32m===========================[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis minor release delivers significant improvements across robustness, concurrency,[m
[32m+[m[32mmultiprocess safety, and performance. Highlights include full fork() safety for shared[m
[32m+[m[32mthread pools and reader caches, race-free lazy initialization of the library and plugins,[m
[32m+[m[32mhardening of frame parsing and orthogonal selections against corrupt or malicious inputs,[m
[32m+[m[32mconsistent frame serialization preserving stored chunks across all storage layouts,[m
[32m+[m[32ma new b2nd sub-box slice extraction API (`b2nd_get_slice_cbuffer_into()`), and widespread[m
[32m+[m[32mSIMD and memory-allocation optimizations.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m* **New public APIs**:[m
[32m+[m[32m  - `b2nd_get_slice_cbuffer_into()`: Extracts an ND slice directly[m
[32m+[m[32m    into a sub-box of an existing, larger C-order destination buffer (e.g. for batch slots,[m
[32m+[m[32m    padded arrays, or multi-channel buffers) without zeroing surrounding memory or allocating[m
[32m+[m[32m    temporaries (#845).[m
[32m+[m[32m  - `blosc2_schunk_insert_buffer()` and `blosc2_schunk_update_buffer()`: Insert or update[m
[32m+[m[32m    uncompressed data into a super-chunk directly, reusing the calling thread's compression[m
[32m+[m[32m    buffers instead of allocating per-chunk temporaries (#868).[m
[32m+[m[32m  - `blosc2_schunk_begin_updates()` and `blosc2_schunk_end_updates()`: Bracket multiple chunk[m
[32m+[m[32m    modifications into a single atomic pass, taking an exclusive lock and compacting any freed[m
[32m+[m[32m    frame space in one efficient pass (#858).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m* **Behaviour change: serializing keeps the chunks as stored, also with a[m
[32m+[m[32m  postfilter.**  `blosc2_schunk_to_buffer()`, `blosc2_schunk_to_buffer_alloc()`,[m
[32m+[m[32m  `blosc2_schunk_to_file()`, `blosc2_schunk_append_file()`, `b2nd_to_cframe()`,[m
[32m+[m[32m  `b2nd_save()` and `b2nd_save_append()` now write the chunks as they are stored[m
[32m+[m[32m  for every storage.  Before, they wrote the postfilter's output for a[m
[32m+[m[32m  super-chunk with a postfilter unless it was an in-memory contiguous frame[m
[32m+[m[32m  (`b2nd_save()` always did), so the result depended on the storage and the[m
[32m+[m[32m  function, and setting the postfilter again on the loaded super-chunk applied[m
[32m+[m[32m  it twice.  Code that loads such a frame without setting the postfilter again[m
[32m+[m[32m  now reads the stored values instead of the postfiltered ones.  To serialize[m
[32m+[m[32m  the postfiltered values, serialize a `blosc2_schunk_copy()` (or `b2nd_copy()`)[m
[32m+[m[32m  of the super-chunk, which applies the postfilter as before (except for[m
[32m+[m[32m  super-chunks with variable-length blocks, whose chunks are always copied as[m
[32m+[m[32m  they are).  Super-chunks without filters give the same frames as before, and[m
[32m+[m[32m  with a prefilter or a postfilter, serializing no longer decompresses and[m
[32m+[m[32m  recompresses every chunk, which makes it much faster (#858).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m* **Robustness & Frame Validation**:[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Fixed a critical out-of-bounds indexing and buffer validation vulnerability in[m
[32m+[m[32m    `b2nd_get_orthogonal_selection()` and `b2nd_set_orthogonal_selection()`. Negative[m
[32m+[m[32m    indices and indices equal to array shape are now rejected, and buffer dimensions[m
[32m+[m[32m    and sizes are properly validated against stride overflows (#864).[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Prevented segmentation faults (SEGV) when copying damaged frames where chunk loading[m
[32m+[m[32m    aborts mid-way: chunk pointers are now calloc'd and checked so the error path[m
[32m+[m[32m    frees only allocated chunks (#869).[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Hardened frame reading against corrupted/damaged files: fixed improper freeing[m
[32m+[m[32m    of mmap buffers in `read_lazy_chunk_bytes()`, prevented NULL pointer dereferences[m
[32m+[m[32m    in `frame_get_lazychunk()` on incomplete reads, validated block sizes against chunk[m
[32m+[m[32m    bounds, checked for 64-bit stride arithmetic overflows, and rejected b2nd metalayers[m
[32m+[m[32m    that contradict super-chunk chunk counts (#871).[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Prevented null-pointer dereferences and crashes when dynamically loading broken[m
[32m+[m[32m    or incomplete filter, codec, or tuner plugins (#873).[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Fixed resource leaks on error paths of `blosc2_create_cctx()` and[m
[32m+[m[32m    `blosc2_create_dctx()`: contexts, preparams, postparams, and mutexes are now[m
[32m+[m[32m    reliably freed when initialization fails (#868).[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Isolated variable-length metalayer (`vlmetalayer`) contents from compression/decompression[m
[32m+[m[32m    filters: prefilters and postfilters now run only on user chunk data, never modifying[m
[32m+[m[32m    metalayers (#857).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m* **Concurrency, Thread Safety & Fork Safety**:[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Initialized the library and dynamic plugins in a thread-safe manner, eliminating races,[m
[32m+[m[32m    deadlocks, and segfaults when worker threads make their first Blosc calls concurrently without[m
[32m+[m[32m    prior `blosc2_init()`: `blosc2_init()`, `blosc2_destroy()`, and `fork()` now synchronize under[m
[32m+[m[32m    a statically initialized lock with acquire/release barriers, dynamic plugins are loaded exactly[m
[32m+[m[32m    once under a plugin lock, and `blosc2_list_compressors()` returns an immutable compile-time[m
[32m+[m[32m    constant (#875).[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Ensured thread-safe lazy initialization of shuffle/bitshuffle implementations across[m
[32m+[m[32m    multiple threads using `pthread_once()` / `InitOnceExecuteOnce()` (#872).[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Added full fork() safety for shared thread pools: child processes cleanly abandon parent[m
[32m+[m[32m    thread pools and start with an empty registry and new epoch, preventing hangs or crashes[m
[32m+[m[32m    when workers are accessed in forked children (#852).[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Synchronized reader cache access across `fork()`: reader cache lock is held across `fork()`[m
[32m+[m[32m    to prevent handle corruption in parent and child processes (#852).[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Isolated read-ahead threads per slice: each concurrent slice read receives its own share[m
[32m+[m[32m    of prefetch threads, avoiding worker thread starvation (#854).[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Cached unused thread pools across context destructions in `release_thread_backend()`[m
[32m+[m[32m    (retaining up to 2 pools), eliminating repeated thread spawn/join overhead in workloads[m
[32m+[m[32m    using short-lived contexts such as single-call Python decompressions (#865).[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Resolved a lock contention regression introduced in 3.5.0 in `parallel_blosc()`:[m
[32m+[m[32m    workers are now woken with `pthread_cond_broadcast()` after unlocking the pool mutex,[m
[32m+[m[32m    restoring multi-threaded scaling on small workloads with few blocks (#878).[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Dropped unused `idle_cv` condition variable in shared thread pools to eliminate a[m
[32m+[m[32m    ThreadSanitizer data race (#859).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m* **Performance & SIMD Optimizations**:[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Accelerated run-length detection in `get_run()` by comparing 64 bytes per iteration[m
[32m+[m[32m    with SSE2 and ARM NEON intrinsics, yielding 5.5%–8% faster compression on repetitive[m
[32m+[m[32m    data while eliminating an unaligned pointer cast (#874).[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Vectorized the final transposition step of bitunshuffle for 1-byte and 2-byte[m
[32m+[m[32m    elements using AVX-512, AVX2, and SSE2 bit-matrix transpositions, accelerating[m
[32m+[m[32m    bitunshuffle for small element sizes (#867).[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Optimized bitshuffle memory usage by reusing the thread context scratch buffer (`tmp4`)[m
[32m+[m[32m    instead of allocating and freeing a temporary buffer per block, eliminating heap trimming[m
[32m+[m[32m    and minor page faults (#860).[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Merged contiguous trailing dimensions in orthogonal selection copies (`copy_block_buffer_data()`),[m
[32m+[m[32m    accelerating channels-last image selections (e.g. `(1, 128, 128, 3)` uint8 blocks) by ~4.7x (#861).[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Merged contiguous dimensions in b2nd box copies (`b2nd_copy_buffer2()`) and zeroing[m
[32m+[m[32m    (`b2nd_zero_box()`), replacing multidimensional loops with single `memcpy`/`memset` runs (#851).[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Accelerated short row copies in `b2nd_copy_buffer2()`: rows up to 64 bytes are copied[m
[32m+[m[32m    with fixed-size moves without `memcpy()` overhead, unified across up to 16 dimensions (#846).[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Skipped decompression of zero and uninitialized special chunks in b2nd slice reads, directly[m
[32m+[m[32m    zeroing destination boxes (or entire slice with `memset` when >= 25% zeros) (#844).[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Improved slice memory efficiency in `b2nd_get_slice()` by reusing the thread-local[m
[32m+[m[32m    scratch buffer (`blosc2_tmp_malloc`/`blosc2_tmp_free`), avoiding repeated malloc/free[m
[32m+[m[32m    cycles and glibc page fault thrashing (#866).[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Kept serial `thread_context` per OS thread instead of reallocating it per context (#849).[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Reused chunk compression buffers across writes in `compress_chunks_into_frame()` (#850).[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Closed frame slice holes once across the entire write instead of per chunk (#847).[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Optimized prefetch cache checking: check only needed blocks of partly read chunks for[m
[32m+[m[32m    page-cache residency, eliminating residency check overhead for cached slices (#862).[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Streamlined frame file opening: open with `fstat()` to avoid `SEEK_END` seeks, request[m
[32m+[m[32m    head and tail hints upon opening with prefetch, and skip advisory start hints on unmapped[m
[32m+[m[32m    stdio frame files (#853, #877).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m* **Documentation & Examples**:[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Added examples demonstrating `blosc2_schunk_insert_buffer()` and `blosc2_schunk_update_buffer()` (#855).[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Added examples demonstrating `blosc2_schunk_begin_updates()` and `blosc2_schunk_end_updates()` (#856).[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Documented open-time hints in `blosc2_set_prefetch()` (#853).[m
