[32m+[m[32m/* One pool per process, guarded by its mutex.  Every slice being read (a batch) gets up to `nthreads` threads of it[m
[32m+[m[32m   at once: the pool grows to `nthreads` threads per batch in its FIFO (at most BLOSC2_PREFETCH_MAX_NTHREADS), and no[m
[32m+[m[32m   batch has more than its `nthreads` pieces in flight.  So N threads of a process that read at the same time get the[m
