[32m+[m[32m#if defined(__linux__)[m
[32m+[m[32m/* Whether the file behind @p fd is on GPFS.  This runs on every read, and on NFS fstatfs() asks the server every time[m
[32m+[m[32m   (0.2 ms) and fstat() at times (0.1 ms after the file's pages were dropped), so each thread keeps the answer for the[m
[32m+[m[32m   last few file systems it read from, by the device of the file from statx() asking for no attributes and not to sync[m
[32m+[m[32m   them, which NFS answers from its cache.  Without statx() (glibc < 2.28) there is no check, and no populating unless[m
[32m+[m[32m   asked for (prefetch_set_populate()). */[m
