[32m+[m[32m# Bitshuffle SIMD optimization measurements[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Scope and implementation[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mBaseline: `6307c47f7b09d80e1f9359191f7acf91271bca68`.[m
[32m+[m[32mHost: Apple M4 Pro, 24 GiB, macOS, Apple Clang 21.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Specialize the full forward/inverse pipelines for 1/2/4/8/16-byte elements.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Forward: byte-shuffle into scratch, then emit each byte plane's bit rows directly[m
[32m+[m[32m  to the final destination. This removes the full-buffer bitrow reorder and skips[m
[32m+[m[32m  the initial copy for one-byte elements.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Inverse: fuse bitrow gathering with independent 8x8 bit transposes in vector[m
[32m+[m[32m  registers, producing byte planes, then use the existing SIMD byte unshuffle.[m
[32m+[m[32m  One-byte elements need neither scratch materialization nor byte unshuffle.[m
[32m+[m[32m- NEON: replace scalar movemask emulation with vector bit transposes; process[m
[32m+[m[32m  128-byte forward tiles with vector stores instead of short scalar stores.[m
[32m+[m[32m- AVX2 retains a 128-bit byte-shuffle stage and uses AVX2 for forward bit packing;[m
[32m+[m[32m  inverse bit reconstruction shares the fused SSE2 helper, followed by AVX2 byte[m
[32m+[m[32m  unshuffle. A tested 256-bit inverse reconstruction was much slower under Rosetta[m
[32m+[m[32m  and was not retained; native x86 tuning remains necessary.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Enable NEON bitshuffle dispatch on AArch64. Previously it was disabled and the[m
[32m+[m[32m  scalar implementation was selected. ARMv7 and non-specialized NEON element sizes[m
[32m+[m[32m  retain their scalar implementation. No format or public API changes.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Native NEON kernel results[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m128,000-byte, cache-resident buffers, one thread. Times are microseconds per[m
[32m+[m[32mcomplete forward/inverse kernel call, including scratch-buffer traffic but not[m
[32m+[m[32mallocation or codecs. Each time is the best of five batches of 4,000 calls.[m
[32m+[m[32m**The baseline is the previously dispatched scalar kernel**, not the slower,[m
[32m+[m[32mdisabled old NEON implementation. Scalar and NEON are timed in the same binary.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| Bytes/type | Shuffle before | After | Speedup | Unshuffle before | After | Speedup |[m
[32m+[m[32m|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|[m
[32m+[m[32m| 1 | 40.792 | 13.252 | 3.08x | 39.286 | 12.970 | 3.03x |[m
[32m+[m[32m| 2 | 41.064 | 15.576 | 2.64x | 39.698 | 15.016 | 2.64x |[m
[32m+[m[32m| 4 | 41.048 | 15.726 | 2.61x | 41.362 | 15.220 | 2.72x |[m
[32m+[m[32m| 8 | 40.828 | 15.605 | 2.62x | 44.594 | 15.254 | 2.92x |[m
[32m+[m[32m| 16 | 40.716 | 16.613 | 2.45x | 53.306 | 16.032 | 3.32x |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## SSE2 and AVX2 under Rosetta[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**These are translated x86 measurements, not native Intel/AMD results.** They[m
[32m+[m[32mvalidate correctness and provide a local comparison only. In particular, large[m
[32m+[m[32mAVX2 inverse improvements reflect Rosetta's translation costs and should not be[m
[32m+[m[32mextrapolated to native AVX2 CPUs. Same timing protocol as NEON. The SSE2 object is[m
