[32m+[m[32m# Review of SHUFFLE, BITSHUFFLE, and SHUFFLE+BYTEDELTA fast paths[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Baseline and scope[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mBaseline: `f1256e391fc1649a6d77e337370c9583c603a670`. Apple M4 Pro,[m
[32m+[m[32m24 GiB RAM, Apple Clang, native ARM64. Python-Blosc2 uses the same source and[m
[32m+[m[32mminiexpr dependency in both isolated packages. This review builds on the[m
[32m+[m[32mrecently enabled NEON bitshuffle, rather than comparing with the old scalar[m
[32m+[m[32mdispatch.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe initial production candidate changes only NEON forward bitshuffle. SHUFFLE,[m
[32m+[m[32mSHUFFLE+BYTEDELTA, codecs, partitions, inverse kernels, Python sources, and[m
[32m+[m[32mdependency pins are identical across the paired measurements.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Review findings[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### SHUFFLE[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe 2-byte NEON path already batches four tiles, the 4-byte path uses LD4, and[m
[32m+[m[32mthe 8-byte path uses a register transpose. The 16-byte path processes eight[m
[32m+[m[32mplanes at a time to avoid too many simultaneous output streams. The inverse[m
[32m+[m[32m8-byte path explicitly uses full-width stores to avoid a known Clang codegen[m
[32m+[m[32mregression. These are already short, load/store-heavy kernels.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe earlier standalone-shuffle investigation established modest constructor[m
[32m+[m[32mimprovements. The earlier fused-transpose investigation tested structured-load[m
[32m+[m[32mreplacement, ZIP butterflies, delta-before-transpose, unrolling, and alternative[m
[32m+[m[32mstores. A roughly 7% isolated four-byte kernel gain failed end-to-end[m
[32m+[m[32mqualification. Repeating those changes without new evidence is not justified.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSHUFFLE is a control in the new constructor measurements. No further[m
[32m+[m[32mSHUFFLE-specific speedup is established by this review.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### SHUFFLE+BYTEDELTA[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe new pair already eliminates the whole intermediate write/read between[m
[32m+[m[32mtranspose and delta, and compile-time plane counts avoid register spills.[m
[32m+[m[32mFusion requires adjacent filters with matching group metadata and preserves[m
[32m+[m[32mthe legacy/fallback cases. Native support is currently for 2/4/8-byte groups.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThere is limited headroom in the forward 4/8-byte NEON pair compared with[m
[32m+[m[32mstandalone SHUFFLE: the delta adds only an extract and subtraction per vector.[m
[32m+[m[32mRemaining constructor time includes source generation, codec work, per-chunk[m
[32m+[m[32msynchronization, and allocation. The pair is also a control in the new runs.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mPossible follow-ups, requiring separate qualification:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- A native AVX2 fused implementation: x86 fusion currently uses SSSE3 even on[m
[32m+[m[32m  AVX2-capable CPUs.[m
[32m+[m[32m- A 16-byte fused implementation, if representative complex/structured-array[m
[32m+[m[32m  workloads justify it; float32/float64 ramps do not test that group size.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Source-generation and dispatch profiling for float32 constructors. In the[m
[32m+[m[32m  screen, float32 three-dimensional linspace is about 174–189 ms across all[m
[32m+[m[32m  filters at 100M elements; improving a filter cannot remove that common cost.[m
[32m+[m[32m  This observation does not identify its exact owner without profiling.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### BITSHUFFLE: a measured opportunity[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe new two-pass implementation still transposes the bits of every byte plane,[m
[32m+[m[32mincluding planes whose bytes are all identical. Floating-point ramps often[m
[32m+[m[32mhave constant sign/exponent bytes and, for integer-valued float64, constant low[m
[32m+[m[32mmantissa bytes.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe candidate probes the first and last 16 bytes of a sufficiently large plane.[m
[32m+[m[32mIf those are uniform, it verifies **every byte** with a vector scan. Only a[m
[32m+[m[32mverified constant plane is emitted as eight zero/one bit rows using `memset`.[m
[32m+[m[32mOther planes use the existing SIMD transpose. This preserves the format and[m
[32m+[m[32mdoes not infer constancy from a sample.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis is a data-dependent optimization, not a universal bitshuffle speedup.[m
[32m+[m[32mRandom planes normally reject at the probes. A nearly constant plane whose[m
[32m+[m[32mendpoints match can pay for an unsuccessful full scan and then the normal[m
[32m+[m[32mtranspose. The initial one-byte, single-interior-difference case was about[m
[32m+[m[32m13–15% slower. The follow-up prefix implementation described below removes this[m
[32m+[m[32mspecific regression.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAdditional x86 review finding: AVX-512 is dispatched ahead of AVX2, but its[m
[32m+[m[32mforward bitshuffle still uses the older three-pass implementation. Porting the[m
[32m+[m[32mtwo-pass design and comparing dispatch choices on actual AVX-512 hardware is[m
[32m+[m[32mworth investigating. Rosetta cannot establish that result.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Measurement protocol[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m`bench/bench_filter_constructors.py` launches isolated before/after workers,[m
[32m+[m[32malternates their execution order, rotates/reverses cell order, and discards one[m
[32m+[m[32mwarm-up per cell per session. It records wall and process CPU times, validates[m
[32m+[m[32msampled values including endpoints/block boundaries, and requires matching[m
[32m+[m[32mcompressed sizes and storage parameters. Only one timed worker runs at a time;[m
[32m+[m[32mbuilds and tests are not run concurrently with constructor measurements.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mWorkloads: `arange(float(n))`, `linspace(0, 1, n)`, and a separate 3-D screen[m
[32m+[m[32mwith shape `(n/1000000, 1000, 1000)`. Dtypes: float32 and float64. Twelve threads.[m
[32m+[m[32mThe 1-D workloads use 16 MB chunks and 128 KB blocks; the 3-D screen uses 16 MB[m
[32m+[m[32mchunks and 80 KB blocks. Partitions are fixed in bytes across dtypes and are[m
[32m+[m[32midentical before/after. Timings include construction and compression, but not[m
[32m+[m[32mvalidation, garbage collection, or result destruction.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe native paired microbenchmark alternates libraries in the same process and[m
[32m+[m[32mreports medians of nine batches of 500 calls following a warm-up. It checks[m
[32m+[m[32mexact transformed-byte equality and includes random, ramp, constant, and[m
[32m+[m[32malmost-constant inputs. A single cache-resident block represents a segment in[m
[32m+[m[32mthe middle of a billion-element ramp, not the entire constructor.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Initial 100M-element screen, clevel 1[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mOne session, three measured repetitions. Useful for screening, not final[m
[32m+[m[32mcross-machine performance claims:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| BITSHUFFLE workload | LZ4 before → after | ZSTD before → after |[m
