[32m+[m[32m### Comparing the three pipelines[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mCandidate timings at clevel 1, one billion float64 elements:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| Constructor | Codec | SHUFFLE | BITSHUFFLE | SHUFFLE+BYTEDELTA |[m
[32m+[m[32m|---|---|---:|---:|---:|[m
[32m+[m[32m| arange | LZ4 | 107.66 ms | 168.24 ms | 110.92 ms |[m
[32m+[m[32m| arange | ZSTD | 121.86 ms | 232.42 ms | 138.78 ms |[m
[32m+[m[32m| linspace | LZ4 | 359.92 ms | 364.62 ms | 140.10 ms |[m
[32m+[m[32m| linspace | ZSTD | 533.14 ms | 498.12 ms | 651.91 ms |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFilter choice remains a time/space tradeoff. For example, float64 linspace with[m
[32m+[m[32mLZ4 is about 2.57x faster with the fused pair than with SHUFFLE alone, and its[m
[32m+[m[32mcompressed size is 105 MB versus 1,060 MB. For ZSTD level 1, the fused pair is[m
[32m+[m[32mslower but stores 176 MB versus SHUFFLE's 346 MB. Codec level therefore matters;[m
[32m+[m[32mthe earlier level-5 results cannot be applied to level 1.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Level-5 cross-check[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mTwo fresh process pairs, eight measured samples per variant, float64, same[m
[32m+[m[32m1-D partitions. These are also initial full-plane candidate measurements:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| Constructor | Codec | SHUFFLE | BITSHUFFLE | SHUFFLE+BYTEDELTA |[m
[32m+[m[32m|---|---|---:|---:|---:|[m
[32m+[m[32m| arange | LZ4 | 108.31 ms | 168.45 ms | 110.99 ms |[m
[32m+[m[32m| arange | ZSTD | 147.23 ms | 555.05 ms | 165.98 ms |[m
[32m+[m[32m| linspace | LZ4 | 328.64 ms | 366.88 ms | 139.21 ms |[m
[32m+[m[32m| linspace | ZSTD | 1357.93 ms | 1178.33 ms | 463.63 ms |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mIncremental BITSHUFFLE speedups at level 5 are 1.258x/1.061x for LZ4[m
[32m+[m[32marange/linspace, and 1.088x/1.010x for ZSTD. ZSTD codec time increasingly[m
[32m+[m[32mdominates, so the same filter optimization produces a smaller end-to-end gain.[m
[32m+[m[32mThe fused pair remains the strongest measured LZ4 linspace choice.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## LZ4-focused follow-up: constant prefixes[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe follow-up stops checking at the first nonconstant 128-byte tile and emits[m
[32m+[m[32mthe verified prefix as bit rows. The existing transpose starts at that tile,[m
[32m+[m[32mnot at the beginning of the plane. It does not rescan/retranspose the already[m
[32m+[m[32mverified prefix, even when the full plane is not constant.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe scan is now implemented in a small private header shared by NEON, SSE2,[m
[32m+[m[32mand AVX2. A minimum byte-plane length of 1,024 avoids row-fill setup costs on[m
[32m+[m[32mtiny planes; for example the initial 128-byte-plane shortcut regressed a[m
[32m+[m[32m1 KB float64 block. Inputs below the cutoff retain the normal SIMD path.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mIn the 128 KB paired kernel comparison, float64 arange improves about 2.04x[m
[32m+[m[32mand linspace 1.34x versus the original optimized baseline. Random-byte kernels[m
[32m+[m[32mremain essentially flat. The one-byte interior-difference case now improves[m
[32m+[m[32mabout 1.56x instead of regressing. The prefix representation and all emitted[m
[32m+[m[32mbytes remain identical to the scalar oracle.[m
[32m+[m
