[31m-## Serialization format[m
[31m-[m
[31m-### Notation[m
[31m-[m
[31m-The msgpack tags used in the formats below:[m
[31m-[m
[31m-- `fixmap`: a fixmap tag whose length is less than or equal to 15.[m
[31m-- `map16` / `map32`: a map tag with a 16-bit or 32-bit length prefix (2 or 4 extra bytes).[m
[31m-- `fixarray`: a fixarray tag whose length is less than or equal to 15.[m
[31m-- `fixstr`: a fixstr tag whose length is less than or equal to 31.[m
[31m-- `str8` / `str16` / `str32`: string tags with an 8-, 16- or 32-bit length prefix.[m
[31m-- `uint`: any of the msgpack unsigned-integer tags. All integers are stored in[m
[31m-  **big-endian** byte order.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-Every tag occupies exactly one byte.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-### Version 1[m
[31m-[m
[31m-Version 1 is the first EmbedStore format; its serialization is implemented in **pure[m
[31m-Python** (python-blosc2). The serialized index is a msgpack map with two fields:[m
[31m-[m
[31m-- `current_offset`: an unsigned integer with the current offset (arena high-water mark).[m
[31m-- `embed_map`: a map from each key (a string) to a nested map with the location:[m
[31m-  - `offset`: the offset of the serialized value.[m
[31m-  - `length`: the length of the serialized value.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-If a value is a remote `C2Array` reference instead of an embedded container, the nested[m
[31m-map uses these keys instead:[m
[31m-[m
[31m-- `urlbase`: the Caterva2 (or other) server URL.[m
[31m-- `path`: the path on the server where the data lives.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-A Python representation of this structure looks like this:[m
[31m-[m
[31m-```python[m
[31m-# `metadata` is another map[m
[31m-metadata["estore_metadata"] = {[m
[31m-    "current_offset": 1234,[m
[31m-    "embed_map": {[m
[31m-        "/first_key": {[m
[31m-            "offset": 0,[m
[31m-            "length": 10,[m
[31m-        },[m
[31m-        "/caterva_data": {[m
[31m-            "urlbase": "catervaserver.com",[m
[31m-            "path": "/on/my/way",[m
[31m-        },[m
[31m-        "/second_key": {[m
[31m-            "offset": 11,[m
[31m-            "length": 20,[m
[31m-        },[m
[31m-    },[m
[31m-}[m
[31m-```[m
[31m-[m
[31m-In msgpack, the first entries above are laid out as follows:[m
[31m-[m
[31m-| Tag / bytes | Meaning |[m
[31m-| ----------- | ------- |[m
[31m-| `fixmap` | Map header with 2 entries |[m
[31m-| `fixstr` `"current_offset"` | Key |[m
[31m-| `uint` `1234` | Value |[m
[31m-| `fixstr` `"embed_map"` | Key |[m
[31m-| `fixmap` | Map header with 3 entries |[m
[31m-| `fixstr` `"/first_key"` | Key |[m
[31m-| `fixmap` | Value map header with 2 entries |[m
[31m-| `fixstr` `"offset"` | Key |[m
[31m-| `uint` `0` | Value |[m
[31m-| `fixstr` `"length"` | Key |[m
[31m-| `uint` `10` | Value |[m
[31m-| `fixstr` `"/caterva_data"` | Key |[m
[31m-| `fixmap` | Value map header with 2 entries |[m
[31m-| `fixstr` `"urlbase"` | Key |[m
[31m-| `fixstr` `"catervaserver.com"` | Value (a string) |[m
[31m-| `fixstr` `"path"` | Key |[m
[31m-| `fixstr` `"/on/my/way"` | Value (a string) |[m
[31m-| `...` | Remaining entries |[m
[31m-[m
[31m-### Version 2[m
[31m-[m
[31m-Version 2 is the format implemented natively in **c-blosc2**[m
[31m-(`blosc/utils/msgpack.c`). It is designed to be smaller and simpler than Version 1:[m
[31m-[m
[31m-- The payload is a **two-element array**: `[current_offset, embed_map]`.[m
[31m-- The first element is `current_offset`, an unsigned integer holding the arena's[m
[31m-  high-water mark (the offset at which the next value will be appended).[m
