[32m+[m[32m/* Replace the frame file underneath an open schunk that has already written[m
[32m+[m[32m   through its cached handle: the next write must land in the replacement (as[m
[32m+[m[32m   it did when every write reopened the path), not in the unlinked old inode. */[m
[32m+[m[32mstatic char* test_replaced_file(void) {[m
